IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pua-my-supply`

-- Public Utilities Act 2001, s 2, ss 21 to 25, 27, 28, 31, 32, 34, 37, 38, 55B and 68B, the consumer's supply -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_public-utilities-act-2001_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `s 2 -- consumer and occupier`

`an owner whose flat is connected but not yet supplied` MEANS `My place` WITH
    `I am supplied with water` IS FALSE
    `my premises are connected to a system of water supply` IS TRUE
    `I am in occupation of the premises` IS FALSE
    `I have the charge, management or control of the premises` IS FALSE
    `I am a lodger` IS FALSE

`a tenant living in the flat` MEANS `My place` WITH
    `I am supplied with water` IS TRUE
    `my premises are connected to a system of water supply` IS FALSE
    `I am in occupation of the premises` IS TRUE
    `I have the charge, management or control of the premises` IS FALSE
    `I am a lodger` IS FALSE

`a lodger renting a room` MEANS `My place` WITH
    `I am supplied with water` IS FALSE
    `my premises are connected to a system of water supply` IS FALSE
    `I am in occupation of the premises` IS TRUE
    `I have the charge, management or control of the premises` IS FALSE
    `I am a lodger` IS TRUE

`a managing agent in charge of a shophouse` MEANS `My place` WITH
    `I am supplied with water` IS FALSE
    `my premises are connected to a system of water supply` IS FALSE
    `I am in occupation of the premises` IS FALSE
    `I have the charge, management or control of the premises` IS TRUE
    `I am a lodger` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `Am I a consumer` `an owner whose flat is connected but not yet supplied`

#ASSERT `Am I the occupier` `a tenant living in the flat`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I the occupier` `a lodger renting a room`
#ASSERT `Am I the occupier` `a managing agent in charge of a shophouse`

§ `ss 21, 22, 23, 34, 37(2) -- cut-off and resumption`

`security asked for 7 days ago and not given` MEANS `My supply` WITH
    `my premises were erected in breach of written law or are ruinous or dangerous` IS FALSE
    `my water service installation is in an unsatisfactory condition` IS FALSE
    `the Board served me a notice to give security` IS TRUE
    `days since the security notice was served` IS 7
    `I have given the security` IS FALSE
    `I am in default in paying a sum due under my supply agreement` IS FALSE
    `the Board is of the opinion that I am responsible for misuse or waste of water` IS FALSE
    `the Board gave me written notice to stop the misuse or waste` IS FALSE
    `the misuse or waste continued after the period in that notice` IS FALSE
    `I neglected to report a pipe wasting water and it is not yet repaired` IS FALSE

`security asked for 8 days ago and not given` MEANS `My supply` WITH
    `my premises were erected in breach of written law or are ruinous or dangerous` IS FALSE
    `my water service installation is in an unsatisfactory condition` IS FALSE
    `the Board served me a notice to give security` IS TRUE
    `days since the security notice was served` IS 8
    `I have given the security` IS FALSE
    `I am in default in paying a sum due under my supply agreement` IS FALSE
    `the Board is of the opinion that I am responsible for misuse or waste of water` IS FALSE
    `the Board gave me written notice to stop the misuse or waste` IS FALSE
    `the misuse or waste continued after the period in that notice` IS FALSE
    `I neglected to report a pipe wasting water and it is not yet repaired` IS FALSE

`a bill in default` MEANS `My supply` WITH
    `my premises were erected in breach of written law or are ruinous or dangerous` IS FALSE
    `my water service installation is in an unsatisfactory condition` IS FALSE
    `the Board served me a notice to give security` IS FALSE
    `days since the security notice was served` IS 0
    `I have given the security` IS FALSE
    `I am in default in paying a sum due under my supply agreement` IS TRUE
    `the Board is of the opinion that I am responsible for misuse or waste of water` IS FALSE
    `the Board gave me written notice to stop the misuse or waste` IS FALSE
    `the misuse or waste continued after the period in that notice` IS FALSE
    `I neglected to report a pipe wasting water and it is not yet repaired` IS FALSE

`waste warned about and stopped in time` MEANS `My supply` WITH
    `my premises were erected in breach of written law or are ruinous or dangerous` IS FALSE
    `my water service installation is in an unsatisfactory condition` IS FALSE
    `the Board served me a notice to give security` IS FALSE
    `days since the security notice was served` IS 0
    `I have given the security` IS FALSE
    `I am in default in paying a sum due under my supply agreement` IS FALSE
    `the Board is of the opinion that I am responsible for misuse or waste of water` IS TRUE
    `the Board gave me written notice to stop the misuse or waste` IS TRUE
    `the misuse or waste continued after the period in that notice` IS FALSE
    `I neglected to report a pipe wasting water and it is not yet repaired` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `May the Board cut off my supply` `security asked for 7 days ago and not given` EQUALS `ss 21, 22, 23 and 34 give the Board no ground to cut off my supply`
#ASSERT `May the Board cut off my supply` `security asked for 8 days ago and not given` EQUALS `the Board may cut off my supply, if it thinks fit`
#ASSERT `May the Board cut off my supply` `a bill in default` EQUALS `the Board may cut off my supply, if it thinks fit`
#ASSERT `May the Board cut off my supply` `waste warned about and stopped in time` EQUALS `ss 21, 22, 23 and 34 give the Board no ground to cut off my supply`

#ASSERT NOT `Have I done what s 37(2) asks before my supply may be resumed` TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 24, 24A, 24B, 32 -- notice before entry`

`an inspection of my occupied flat without my consent` MEANS `The entry` WITH
    `why` IS `to survey, inspect or execute authorised work`
    `my premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy` IS TRUE
    `I consent to the entry` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has declared my class of premises liable to inspection at any time` IS FALSE
    `the Board considers immediate action necessary for a s 24B reason` IS FALSE

`an inspection of my occupied flat with my consent` MEANS `The entry` WITH
    `why` IS `to survey, inspect or execute authorised work`
    `my premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy` IS TRUE
    `I consent to the entry` IS TRUE
    `the Minister has declared my class of premises liable to inspection at any time` IS FALSE
    `the Board considers immediate action necessary for a s 24B reason` IS FALSE

`laying a new main through my garden` MEANS `The entry` WITH
    `why` IS `to lay or install mains, pipes, meters or water installations`
    `my premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy` IS TRUE
    `I consent to the entry` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has declared my class of premises liable to inspection at any time` IS FALSE
    `the Board considers immediate action necessary for a s 24B reason` IS FALSE

`laying a main in a burst-pipe emergency` MEANS `The entry` WITH
    `why` IS `to lay or install mains, pipes, meters or water installations`
    `my premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy` IS TRUE
    `I consent to the entry` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has declared my class of premises liable to inspection at any time` IS FALSE
    `the Board considers immediate action necessary for a s 24B reason` IS TRUE

`storing materials on my land beside the works` MEANS `The entry` WITH
    `why` IS `to work on premises within 100 metres of its works`
    `my premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy` IS FALSE
    `I consent to the entry` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has declared my class of premises liable to inspection at any time` IS FALSE
    `the Board considers immediate action necessary for a s 24B reason` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `How much notice must I be given before the Board enters my premises` `an inspection of my occupied flat without my consent` EQUALS `at least 6 hours' notice, unless I consent`
#ASSERT `How much notice must I be given before the Board enters my premises` `an inspection of my occupied flat with my consent` EQUALS `none stated: entry at reasonable hours or at a time agreed with me`
#ASSERT `How much notice must I be given before the Board enters my premises` `laying a new main through my garden` EQUALS `at least 14 days' written notice`
#ASSERT `How much notice must I be given before the Board enters my premises` `laying a main in a burst-pipe emergency` EQUALS `none: the Board may enter immediately and without notice`
#ASSERT `How much notice must I be given before the Board enters my premises` `storing materials on my land beside the works` EQUALS `at least 7 days' written notice`

§ `ss 24A, 27, 28 -- what I can recover from the Board`

#ASSERT `What can I recover from the Board` `my supply failed, was delayed, interrupted or restricted` EQUALS (JUST `nothing: the Act excludes the Board's liability`)
#ASSERT `What can I recover from the Board` `the Board reduced my supply because its water was insufficient` EQUALS (JUST `a proportionate abatement of the sum I agreed to pay for the supply`)
#ASSERT `What can I recover from the Board` `the Board entered and occupied my premises to lay pipes or meters` EQUALS NOTHING

